= Chapter 1

== 1.1 Tech's Techtonic Shift - Radically Changing Business Landscapes
- Many companies have grown and became huge businesses throughout the decade. 
    - Google and Apple were barely known and now are some of the biggest companies in the world. 
- Some factors have affected the progression of techonology, such as #text(weight: "bold")[Moore's Law].
    - Moore's Law is the idea that every two or so year, techonological advancements would double.
- Social media have became a huge part of society, impreoving sales and marketing. 
    - Causes some ethical issues, since privacy is now a concern.
- Globalization has also affected nations. China used to be closed off and offline. Now they have more Internet users than any other country.
- In terms of coding, some companies such as IBM and Oracle would pay programmers to write codes. Now, open source softwares has drastically changed the programming environment.

== 1.2 It's Your Revolution
- Technology and business is scary. However, many of the world's most successful technology firms, such as Microsoft, were created by young individuals.
- Bill Gates left college during his undergrad to create Microsoft.
    - In my opinion, he did not create Microsoft from the ground up. He had many help, and most importantly, he had money.

== 1.3 Geek Up - Tech is Everywhere and You'll Need It to Thrive
- During the start of the prior decade, a concern was brought up that tech jobs would be less valuable and not needed.
    - This concern was due to the increase of outcourced materials.
    - This concern was also wrong, since it turns out tech jobs was #text(weight: "bold")[highly sought after].
    - As technology evolved, tech jobs continued to be required. 
- Moore's Law is behind fast, cheap computing. 
    - As computing gets faster and cheaper, it will be everywhere (ex: phone).
- As technology continues to become faster and cheaper, tech skills will be embedded inside more job functions. 
    - Even if you are not looking to go into tech, tech is still part of you job, whether you like it or not.

#text(weight: "bold")[Finance]

- In terms of #text(weight: "bold")[finance], many finance students will look into investment banking.
    - Investment bankers work on IPOs or public stock offers, which will help value companies the first time these firms wish to sell their stock on the public market.
        - IPOs need new firms, and the tech industry is something that will sprout new businesses very fast.
        - Other investment bankers will be involved in deals that tech firms will also be active in. 
- Leading tech firms would go and acquire new firms.
    - Ex: Cisco acquired 48 firms in the prior decade; Oracle bought 5 firms in 2009. 
- Other finance people would look to invest in tech firms to add to their portfolios and having a tech role as part of their investment.
- Modern finance would not exist without tech; deals are made digitally and funds are transferred online.

#pagebreak()
#text(weight: "bold")[Accounting]

- An accountant's career is built upon a foundation of technology. 
- Numbers are all recorded, stored, and reported by information systems. The reliability of any audit is tied to the reliability of the technology.
- With an increase in regulation means an importance of making sure accountants are correct. 
- With how focused on tech the accountanting firms are, the tech division make up a huge portion of the firm.

#text(weight: "bold")[Marketing]

- Technology has vastly changed how marketing was. 
- Nowadays, the Internet is the main form of marketing. Online channels have ways to track consumer activities.
- Firms are investing less in print, radio, and television and more so in the Web.
- Technology such as the iPhone and iPod has become a mainstream way of tracking and reaching consumers.
- Rise of social media has made it a part of marketing, with social media being used to generate sales and improve reputations.
- Search Engine Marketing (SEM), search engine optimization (SEO), customer relationship management (CRM), personalization systems, and a sensitivity to managing the delicate balance between gathering and leveraging data and respecting consumer privacy are central components for marketing.

#text(weight: "bold")[Operations]
- Tech is very important for operations. A firm's operations management function is focused on producing goods and services, and technology helps produce high quality products. 

#text(weight: "bold")[Human Resources]

- Technology helps firms by connecting employees together. 
    - Social networks, wikis, and messaging systems accelerate the ability of a firm to organize and work together. 
    - Technology can be used by HR for employee training, screening, and evaluation. 
- Technology has also shaped the way that the hiring process is done. 
    - information systems now search across databases to look for specific skill sets to recruit talents. 
    - Job seekers now write resumes with specific keywords that will allow the datase search program to notice them better.

#text(weight: "bold")[The Law]

- Many areas of law and corporate law involve technologies. 
- Intellectual property, patents, piracy, privacy. 
